From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:03:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tls: include inet headers before OpenSSL on QNX

openssl.c uses struct in6_addr and inet_pton() to tell IP addresses from
host names. They are declared in <netinet/in.h> and <arpa/inet.h>, which the
QNX OpenSSL and libc headers do not include transitively, so the file does
not compile.

Include both headers explicitly on QNX.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/tls/openssl.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/tls/openssl.c b/src/tls/openssl.c
index 8d8eb16..6fc7679 100644
--- a/src/tls/openssl.c
+++ b/src/tls/openssl.c
@@ -27,6 +27,11 @@
 #include <fluent-bit/tls/flb_tls.h>
 #include <fluent-bit/tls/flb_tls_info.h>
 
+#ifdef __QNXNTO__
+#include <netinet/in.h>
+#include <arpa/inet.h>
+#endif
+
 #include <openssl/ssl.h>
 #include <openssl/err.h>
 #include <openssl/opensslv.h>
